1
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:38,840
ADAPTED FROM <i>THE EARLY SPRING</i> ON JJWXC.NET
AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

3
00:02:22,040 --> 00:02:25,080
SNOW FALLS WITH YOU BESIDE ME

4
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:37,760
LUAN NIAN

5
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:44,040
<i>Open the door.</i>

6
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,920
We're going to the hospital.

7
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,080
I'm not going.

8
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:35,920
Your face is burning red,
and you won't go to the hospital?

9
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,080
Do you have a death wish?

10
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:17,640
I really don't need to go to the hospital.

11
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:20,240
I'll be fine after some rest.

12
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:23,720
Fine.

13
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:26,680
I'll check the company system
for your emergency contact

14
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:29,360
and inform your family.

15
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:32,320
If you suffer any complications
or accidents later,

16
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:33,240
the company won't be liable.

17
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:48,600
Your hand's burning.

18
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:10,920
Stop being stubborn. Let's go.

19
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:45,040
The doctor said it was a mild case
of mycoplasma pneumonia.

20
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:47,600
A cough and a slight fever.

21
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:50,560
Some congee should be fine, right?

22
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:54,520
It's not me. I'm asking for a friend.

23
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:56,840
Thanks.

24
00:05:58,240 --> 00:05:59,760
Thank you, Dr. Liang.

25
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:06,960
You're awake.

26
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:09,240
Come eat.

27
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,600
Thank you, Mr. Luan.

28
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:31,400
Drop the formalities.

29
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:34,560
Don't you get tired
of addressing me like that?

30
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:37,360
I…

31
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:49,040
Did you burn your hand?

32
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:50,680
Did you put anything on it?

33
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:54,200
Don't worry about it. Eat.

34
00:07:58,520 --> 00:07:59,840
I'm feeling much better.

35
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:02,280
Could you take me home?

36
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:04,280
I don't want to impose.

37
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:06,920
Why are you acting like a stranger?

38
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:16,120
We dated, after all.

39
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:18,640
You don't need to feel bad
about letting me take care of you.

40
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:25,880
I want to go home.

41
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:28,680
I want…

42
00:08:33,880 --> 00:08:35,440
to end this relationship.

43
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:42,000
We can.

44
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:47,120
Once you're better.

45
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:03,640
<i>Later, when I looked back</i>
<i>on who I was then,</i>

46
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:09,240
<i>I couldn't explain</i>
<i>why I made that decision.</i>

47
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:15,080
<i>Why do people always do</i>
<i>such foolish things</i>

48
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:16,560
<i>when they're young?</i>

49
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:24,600
<i>How could something</i>
<i>that began like that ever end well?</i>

50
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:30,640
<i>I acted as if foolish choices</i>
<i>came without a price.</i>

51
00:09:42,560 --> 00:09:43,720
You sweated from the fever.

52
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:45,040
Go take a shower.

53
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:48,360
You need proper rest to recover.

54
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:55,800
Come on.

55
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:10,960
Did you prepare all this for me?

56
00:10:13,680 --> 00:10:14,680
Other women left them here.

57
00:10:16,160 --> 00:10:17,760
Label them when you use them.

58
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:20,840
That way, the next woman who comes over

59
00:10:21,880 --> 00:10:23,480
won't use or wear the wrong things.

60
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,640
These match my prescription.

61
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:30,160
What a coincidence.

62
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:00,000
Come sit down.

63
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:16,520
What are you covering up?

64
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:18,120
I've seen it all before.

65
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:25,320
Why are you always so cutting?

66
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:29,320
Are you like this with everyone
or only with me?

67
00:11:49,280 --> 00:11:53,600
You only said you wanted to end things
because you were angry, right?

68
00:11:57,560 --> 00:11:58,800
I meant it.

69
00:12:05,480 --> 00:12:06,320
Really?

70
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:39,520
It's snowing.

71
00:13:07,640 --> 00:13:08,520
Let's go watch it.

72
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:34,800
It's cold.

73
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:38,240
Don't end this.

74
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:40,560
Or we'll freeze
into ice sculptures together.

75
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:51,520
Could you be more childish?

76
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:52,720
I'm still sick.

77
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:57,120
Then don't break up with me.

78
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:31,280
There were so many gift boxes
in your trunk.

79
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:34,440
Were they meant for other women?

80
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:41,840
Shang Zhitao,

81
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:46,200
do you know how
luxury-brand pre-spend works?

82
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:58,640
I don't want to know anything,
including you.

83
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:08,760
You can take your time getting
to know me once you're better.

84
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:26,720
SHAANXI <i>GUOKUI</i> BUNS

85
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:27,640
Mom.

86
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:30,520
<i>Did you get the buns?</i>

87
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:32,680
I did. They're delicious.

88
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:35,480
<i>We don't have much worth sending.</i>

89
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:37,240
<i>But I know you like them,</i>

90
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:40,800
<i>so I sent extra for you</i>
<i>to share with your roommates.</i>

91
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:42,080
<i>Is it enough?</i>

92
00:15:42,160 --> 00:15:44,520
Yes. Don't worry.

93
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:45,920
<i>About the house,</i>

94
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:48,360
<i>your father still thinks we should buy it.</i>

95
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:51,800
<i>Your sister's grown up.</i>

96
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:53,320
<i>It really isn't convenient.</i>

97
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:56,920
Mom, what about the money
I just sent home?

98
00:15:57,720 --> 00:15:58,920
Did Dad take it again?

99
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,160
<i>Give me the phone. I'll talk to him.</i>

100
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:05,160
<i>Listen. That place has a lot of buyers,</i>

101
00:16:05,240 --> 00:16:06,320
<i>and it's a bargain.</i>

102
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:08,800
<i>We won't get another chance like this.</i>

103
00:16:08,880 --> 00:16:10,720
<i>I'm still 30,000 yuan short.</i>
<i>Send it over right away.</i>

104
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:12,920
<i>Don't talk to him like that.</i>

105
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,720
<i>I know life in Beijing isn't easy for you,</i>

106
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:18,840
<i>but we want to buy a bigger place</i>

107
00:16:18,920 --> 00:16:20,800
<i>and put it</i>
<i>in your and your sister's names.</i>

108
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:23,080
<i>That way, you'll both</i>
<i>have something to fall back on.</i>

109
00:16:23,160 --> 00:16:24,680
<i>Don't bother explaining.</i>

110
00:16:24,760 --> 00:16:25,920
<i>Tell him to send the money now.</i>

111
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,440
<i>Hang up and go cook.</i>

112
00:16:41,920 --> 00:16:45,440
TRANSFER: RMB 30,000

113
00:16:49,480 --> 00:16:51,600
TRANSFER SUCCESSFUL

114
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:11,560
<i>What? Pneumonia?</i>

115
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:12,839
<i>Are you OK?</i>

116
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:15,079
Yes. I'm almost recovered.

117
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:18,240
<i>So you're staying at Luan Nian's now?</i>

118
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:20,760
<i>Are you two back together?</i>

119
00:17:20,839 --> 00:17:22,319
I'VE GONE TO THE SUPERMARKET
I'LL BE BACK SOON

120
00:17:26,160 --> 00:17:27,720
He's been taking good care of me.

121
00:17:28,240 --> 00:17:29,680
He's done everything he can.

122
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:33,320
He rushed back
to take care of you, his girlfriend.

123
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:35,880
<i>He is into you.</i>

124
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:39,880
I can't bring myself to ask
about him and Zang Yao.

125
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:44,840
I'll leave it at that.

126
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:47,120
I don't want to dig any deeper.

127
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:50,720
Take your time.

128
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:54,360
<i>Some things can't be rushed.</i>

129
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:59,320
Leaving some questions unasked may
make a relationship last longer, right?

130
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:01,720
You're right.

131
00:18:04,920 --> 00:18:07,680
I have to go. I think he's back.

132
00:18:48,360 --> 00:18:49,920
Your friend's here.

133
00:18:51,520 --> 00:18:53,040
Why are you here?

134
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:00,880
Drinking in broad daylight?

135
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:04,120
Why can't I? I drink when I feel like it.

136
00:19:05,800 --> 00:19:06,800
Want some?

137
00:19:07,840 --> 00:19:08,680
I…

138
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:11,520
- I should go home.
- Why?

139
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:16,800
Are you fully recovered?

140
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:21,800
I'll make you some soup later.

141
00:19:23,600 --> 00:19:26,000
It'd be awkward with me here.

142
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:30,800
She's the one who's intruding.

143
00:19:37,400 --> 00:19:39,040
So she's your new girlfriend?

144
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:41,920
- Yes.
- No.

145
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:49,960
You two really aren't on the same page.

146
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:55,920
Maybe you should change
the water in the tank.

147
00:19:56,520 --> 00:19:57,520
Why?

148
00:19:58,760 --> 00:20:00,000
She threw up in it.

149
00:20:02,040 --> 00:20:03,360
Zang Yao.

150
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,800
Shang Zhitao.

151
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:19,400
That's a pretty name.

152
00:20:24,280 --> 00:20:25,520
How do you put up with Luan Nian?

153
00:20:25,600 --> 00:20:26,840
Look at him.

154
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:30,120
Even at home, he looks like
he's chairing a board meeting.

155
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:35,200
What kind of rare fish
is it that you treasure so much?

156
00:20:35,280 --> 00:20:37,720
If it dies, I'll buy you ten more.

157
00:20:38,880 --> 00:20:41,320
If you can't make conversation, say less.

158
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:43,880
Hongqi is his baby.

159
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:45,600
Sometimes he talks to it.

160
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:48,040
What are you talking about?

161
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:52,240
I heard you. You told it to swim faster.

162
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:58,080
We've known each other for over 20 years.

163
00:20:58,160 --> 00:21:01,040
He's always been quiet
and never liked talking much.

164
00:21:01,120 --> 00:21:03,040
So he's been confiding in his fish.

165
00:21:03,120 --> 00:21:06,360
I've been away so long
that I understand you less and less.

166
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:10,280
How about this?

167
00:21:10,360 --> 00:21:13,960
Let's play a game we used to play as kids.

168
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:16,000
Rock-paper-scissors, then questions.

169
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:18,520
Whoever loses can either answer a question

170
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:19,880
or take a flick to the forehead.

171
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:22,280
You know how to play, right?

172
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:26,040
Come on. Rock, paper, scissors.

173
00:21:30,880 --> 00:21:31,720
You first.

174
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:33,680
Why did you suddenly come back to China?

175
00:21:33,760 --> 00:21:36,680
I broke up with my British boyfriend.

176
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:39,080
Then I met a guy from Guangzhou
and followed him there.

177
00:21:39,680 --> 00:21:40,760
You certainly kept busy.

178
00:21:42,360 --> 00:21:45,320
Will you take a flick to the forehead
or answer a question?

179
00:21:46,360 --> 00:21:47,360
I'll answer a question.

180
00:21:50,320 --> 00:21:51,720
Is anyone pursuing you right now?

181
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:55,200
No.

182
00:21:57,640 --> 00:21:59,080
That's normal. Nothing to be ashamed of.

183
00:22:00,200 --> 00:22:04,320
Some people go their whole lives
without anyone ever pursuing them.

184
00:22:08,720 --> 00:22:10,040
I have been pursued.

185
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:12,640
My ex-boyfriend loved me very much.

186
00:22:12,720 --> 00:22:14,520
Then why did he break up with you?

187
00:22:17,400 --> 00:22:19,560
- Again.
- Come on.

188
00:22:20,160 --> 00:22:21,320
Rock, paper, scissors.

189
00:22:23,080 --> 00:22:23,920
You again.

190
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:27,000
Still answering a question?

191
00:22:28,920 --> 00:22:29,720
I'll take the flick.

192
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:31,520
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

193
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:41,240
Come here.

194
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:48,320
What's wrong? You chose the flick.

195
00:22:48,920 --> 00:22:50,920
I didn't think you'd flick me that hard.

196
00:22:52,240 --> 00:22:53,960
When we were kids,
Luan Nian could flick my forehead

197
00:22:54,040 --> 00:22:55,800
hard enough to send an eraser flying.

198
00:22:55,880 --> 00:22:57,720
He never went easy on girls.

199
00:22:59,160 --> 00:23:00,960
I thought you'd go easier on me.

200
00:23:02,440 --> 00:23:03,400
Let me see.

201
00:23:04,680 --> 00:23:05,600
I'm fine.

202
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:08,120
There, there.

203
00:23:09,960 --> 00:23:11,720
Again. Come on.

204
00:23:12,360 --> 00:23:13,800
Rock, paper, scissors.

205
00:23:20,040 --> 00:23:21,840
You know Luan Nian

206
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:23,800
has a crescent-shaped scar
on his left leg, right?

207
00:23:25,560 --> 00:23:26,600
He…

208
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:28,240
He does?

209
00:23:28,760 --> 00:23:30,960
- Do you know how he got it?
- From running.

210
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:33,000
Nonsense.

211
00:23:33,080 --> 00:23:35,360
When I was seven, I took you
climbing a wall to raid a bird's nest.

212
00:23:35,440 --> 00:23:36,640
Zang Yao.

213
00:23:37,280 --> 00:23:39,800
Fine. I'll talk about something else.

214
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:40,720
His mom said

215
00:23:40,800 --> 00:23:43,920
that by the time he was seven or eight,
he already acted like a grown-up,

216
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:45,040
always frowning,

217
00:23:45,760 --> 00:23:48,280
never truly interested in anything,
and impossible to please.

218
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:52,920
You're nothing like Dr. Liang
or your father.

219
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:54,640
Were you adopted?

220
00:24:00,560 --> 00:24:01,560
How about another round?

221
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:04,160
Sure.

222
00:24:04,240 --> 00:24:05,800
Rock, paper, scissors.

223
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:08,840
Forehead flick.

224
00:24:27,040 --> 00:24:27,880
That was gentle.

225
00:24:39,240 --> 00:24:40,840
When are you two getting married?

226
00:24:41,920 --> 00:24:43,120
We don't have any plans yet.

227
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:46,280
I'm warning you.

228
00:24:46,360 --> 00:24:47,920
Don't say anything to my mom.

229
00:24:49,320 --> 00:24:52,280
I was asking on Dr. Liang's behalf.

230
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:54,160
Really. She's always asking me
to set you up with someone.

231
00:24:54,840 --> 00:24:55,960
She says with your personality,

232
00:24:56,040 --> 00:24:57,480
you'll bottle everything up
until it kills you.

233
00:25:12,360 --> 00:25:13,440
Boring.

234
00:25:16,760 --> 00:25:20,320
Well, I hope you two make it all the way.

235
00:25:32,920 --> 00:25:34,880
I'm meeting my girls at the bar. Bye.

236
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:07,080
<i>I only wanted us to be family</i>

237
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:09,560
<i>and best friends.</i>

238
00:26:58,680 --> 00:26:59,640
Take your medicine.

239
00:27:08,560 --> 00:27:11,440
When your ex flicked you on the forehead,
was he gentler than I was?

240
00:27:20,600 --> 00:27:22,600
I don't know you as well as Zang Yao does,

241
00:27:22,680 --> 00:27:24,600
and we don't share as many memories.

242
00:27:24,680 --> 00:27:27,160
Let me see the scar she mentioned.

243
00:27:27,240 --> 00:27:28,120
Shang Zhitao.

244
00:27:59,520 --> 00:28:00,600
Was Mount Tai fun?

245
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:05,200
Yes.

246
00:28:06,280 --> 00:28:07,400
More fun than being with me?

247
00:28:22,200 --> 00:28:23,760
Do you hold a grudge over everything?

248
00:28:24,360 --> 00:28:25,640
I went with my roommates.

249
00:28:25,720 --> 00:28:27,840
We're very close,

250
00:28:27,920 --> 00:28:31,800
so we often do things together as a group.

251
00:28:35,480 --> 00:28:38,360
Are group outings more fun
than being with me?

252
00:28:38,960 --> 00:28:40,600
Are you fun?

253
00:28:41,720 --> 00:28:42,560
No.

254
00:28:43,240 --> 00:28:44,760
I'm not cheerful.

255
00:28:44,840 --> 00:28:48,720
I have no empathy and no soft side.

256
00:28:49,320 --> 00:28:51,280
At least you know yourself.

257
00:28:56,760 --> 00:28:57,760
You do have a soft side.

258
00:28:58,600 --> 00:29:00,080
You have friends,

259
00:29:00,680 --> 00:29:02,840
people you travel with,

260
00:29:02,920 --> 00:29:06,320
and even a childhood sweetheart.

261
00:29:06,400 --> 00:29:07,440
Isn't that right?

262
00:29:11,800 --> 00:29:12,640
Come.

263
00:29:21,320 --> 00:29:22,680
Zang Yao is a few years younger than me.

264
00:29:23,680 --> 00:29:25,080
She was sickly as a child,

265
00:29:25,160 --> 00:29:26,920
and my mom often
wrote prescriptions for her.

266
00:29:28,480 --> 00:29:29,800
Later, my parents went abroad.

267
00:29:30,960 --> 00:29:34,560
Her mom was a great cook,
so I often ate at their place.

268
00:29:36,320 --> 00:29:39,880
Your parents went abroad
without taking you?

269
00:29:41,520 --> 00:29:43,040
They went abroad for business.

270
00:29:43,640 --> 00:29:44,480
I didn't want to go.

271
00:29:44,560 --> 00:29:46,400
Are they back now?

272
00:29:48,160 --> 00:29:49,600
But we rarely get to see each other.

273
00:29:50,440 --> 00:29:51,640
Not even during Chinese New Year?

274
00:29:51,720 --> 00:29:53,600
It's almost here.

275
00:29:54,200 --> 00:29:56,480
Once the holiday starts,
I'm going back home.

276
00:29:59,040 --> 00:29:59,960
Shang Zhitao.

277
00:30:01,480 --> 00:30:02,960
When we see each other next year,

278
00:30:03,560 --> 00:30:05,680
I hope you'll call me something different.

279
00:30:08,240 --> 00:30:12,000
What do you want me to call you?

280
00:30:14,480 --> 00:30:15,840
Just call me Luan Nian.

281
00:30:20,840 --> 00:30:22,000
Luan…

282
00:30:24,160 --> 00:30:25,000
Luan Nian.

283
00:30:29,640 --> 00:30:30,560
Luan Nian.

284
00:30:33,760 --> 00:30:34,840
Don't tempt me.

285
00:30:36,520 --> 00:30:37,360
You're still sick.

286
00:30:50,800 --> 00:30:52,120
Actually,

287
00:30:53,240 --> 00:30:56,640
I think it's nice
just lying here like this,

288
00:30:58,760 --> 00:30:59,760
without doing anything.

289
00:31:04,560 --> 00:31:05,400
What's nice about it?

290
00:31:39,320 --> 00:31:40,280
TO-DO LIST
1. LEARN TO DRIVE 2. IMPROVE MY ENGLISH

291
00:31:40,360 --> 00:31:41,240
3. MAKE AT LEAST THREE FRIENDS
4. PASS PROBATION AND GET PROMOTED TO SAE

292
00:31:48,120 --> 00:31:50,840
5. CAREER GOAL: ACCOUNT MANAGER

293
00:31:52,880 --> 00:31:54,560
Did you get your year-end bonus?

294
00:31:55,640 --> 00:31:56,680
Check your email.

295
00:32:01,360 --> 00:32:02,600
That's so much money!

296
00:32:02,680 --> 00:32:04,480
The more, the better.

297
00:32:04,560 --> 00:32:05,600
Get a grip, silly.

298
00:32:06,440 --> 00:32:09,560
HR just announced
a company retreat in Phuket.

299
00:32:10,640 --> 00:32:12,160
Phuket?

300
00:32:15,480 --> 00:32:16,920
- Here.
- No, I can't.

301
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:19,400
Just take it. Once your mentor,
always your mentor.

302
00:32:20,400 --> 00:32:21,240
Happy Chinese New Year.

303
00:32:33,000 --> 00:32:34,360
<i>I'm grateful to Lime</i>

304
00:32:36,560 --> 00:32:39,080
<i>and to myself for working so hard.</i>

305
00:32:39,160 --> 00:32:40,000
GOOD LUCK ALWAYS

306
00:32:40,080 --> 00:32:42,680
<i>My job gave me the chance to work</i>
<i>at the forefront of the industry</i>

307
00:32:43,280 --> 00:32:45,840
<i>and see my efforts rewarded.</i>

308
00:32:47,760 --> 00:32:48,640
<i>I'm also grateful to Luan Nian.</i>

309
00:32:50,120 --> 00:32:51,600
<i>Thank you for your kindness,</i>

310
00:32:52,240 --> 00:32:53,760
<i>for always being strict,</i>

311
00:32:53,840 --> 00:32:56,920
<i>and for pushing me</i>
<i>to grow in my own way.</i>

312
00:33:03,800 --> 00:33:06,520
JANUARY 2014, HARBIN

313
00:33:08,520 --> 00:33:10,120
I LOVE HARBIN

314
00:33:14,480 --> 00:33:15,520
CENTRAL AVENUE

315
00:33:15,600 --> 00:33:16,880
OLD COUPLE'S TAVERN

316
00:33:16,960 --> 00:33:19,160
Dad, I'll have a drink with you tonight.

317
00:33:19,920 --> 00:33:21,400
I'll join in too.

318
00:33:21,480 --> 00:33:22,720
You can barely hold your liquor.

319
00:33:22,800 --> 00:33:23,720
Just have a sip.

320
00:33:24,680 --> 00:33:25,800
- Cheers.
- Happy Chinese New Year!

321
00:33:25,880 --> 00:33:27,680
- Happy Chinese New Year!
- Happy Chinese New Year.

322
00:33:28,560 --> 00:33:30,080
Easy on the drinks.

323
00:33:30,160 --> 00:33:31,200
That's strong.

324
00:33:31,840 --> 00:33:35,200
Sweetheart, try the soup I made for you.

325
00:33:35,280 --> 00:33:36,480
It's been simmering all afternoon.

326
00:33:36,560 --> 00:33:38,200
It smells amazing.

327
00:33:38,720 --> 00:33:40,360
Here. Try it.

328
00:33:40,440 --> 00:33:41,920
All right.

329
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:43,840
- You have some too.
- OK.

330
00:33:43,920 --> 00:33:45,760
Since when did you become
such a great cook?

331
00:33:45,840 --> 00:33:46,680
See?

332
00:33:46,760 --> 00:33:49,400
If Michelin knew,
they'd be giving you a star.

333
00:33:51,040 --> 00:33:55,360
Your auntie next door has a nephew
who's a programmer in Beijing.

334
00:33:55,440 --> 00:33:58,160
His hair is really thick.

335
00:33:58,240 --> 00:34:01,960
And his face is chiseled

336
00:34:02,040 --> 00:34:04,040
- like a European statue.
- Mom…

337
00:34:04,120 --> 00:34:05,000
Give it a rest.

338
00:34:05,080 --> 00:34:06,880
A European statue?

339
00:34:06,960 --> 00:34:09,600
Exactly. Besides, I want to focus on work.

340
00:34:09,679 --> 00:34:11,360
I'm not looking to date right now.

341
00:34:11,440 --> 00:34:13,520
- All right, let me name the dishes.
- Look at you…

342
00:34:13,600 --> 00:34:16,800
We've got <i>Disanxian</i>, sweet-and-sour pork,

343
00:34:16,880 --> 00:34:20,760
and your favorite, blood sausage!

344
00:34:20,840 --> 00:34:22,719
- Dig in.
- Eat.

345
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:28,639
The Spring Festival
is always livelier at home.

346
00:34:28,719 --> 00:34:30,040
Everything feels so festive.

347
00:34:30,120 --> 00:34:31,960
- Stop watching and eat.
- Come on.

348
00:34:34,280 --> 00:34:35,320
Eat.

349
00:34:35,400 --> 00:34:36,600
LUAN NIAN, HAPPY CHINESE NEW YEAR
WISHING YOU ALL THE BEST THIS YEAR

350
00:34:36,679 --> 00:34:37,880
It smells amazing.

351
00:34:37,960 --> 00:34:39,120
Dig in, sweetheart.

352
00:34:39,199 --> 00:34:40,239
Have some blood sausage.

353
00:34:41,600 --> 00:34:43,080
Just looking at you makes me happy.

354
00:34:48,040 --> 00:34:49,400
Mom, this is so good.

355
00:34:49,480 --> 00:34:50,320
Try some.

356
00:34:56,360 --> 00:34:58,680
<i>Luan Nian, Happy Chinese New Year.</i>

357
00:34:59,360 --> 00:35:01,680
<i>Wishing you all the best this year.</i>

358
00:35:10,680 --> 00:35:13,200
Aren't you hot

359
00:35:13,280 --> 00:35:15,560
- wearing a turtleneck indoors?
- No.

360
00:35:16,480 --> 00:35:17,800
Here, have some fruit.

361
00:35:18,440 --> 00:35:19,280
Here.

362
00:35:23,080 --> 00:35:25,720
Are you hiding something from me?

363
00:35:26,360 --> 00:35:28,680
- Like what?
- Like what?

364
00:35:29,480 --> 00:35:30,920
Don't walk away.

365
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:32,400
I'm asking you.

366
00:35:32,480 --> 00:35:33,360
Go ahead.

367
00:35:34,200 --> 00:35:37,440
Are you seeing someone?

368
00:35:38,680 --> 00:35:40,320
Are you really that eager for me to date,

369
00:35:40,400 --> 00:35:42,600
get married, and give you a granddaughter?

370
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:44,600
Why not a grandson?

371
00:35:45,920 --> 00:35:46,920
I prefer a girl.

372
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:49,280
Of course, a granddaughter
would be better.

373
00:35:49,360 --> 00:35:50,280
I'd love that.

374
00:35:51,200 --> 00:35:53,280
Don't change the subject.
Are you seeing someone?

375
00:35:55,440 --> 00:35:56,680
I am.

376
00:35:57,280 --> 00:35:58,360
Really?

377
00:35:58,440 --> 00:36:00,800
What does she do?

378
00:36:00,880 --> 00:36:02,280
What's her personality like?

379
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:03,960
What does she look like?

380
00:36:04,040 --> 00:36:06,960
She's easy on the eyes,
has a great personality,

381
00:36:07,040 --> 00:36:07,960
and works a regular office job.

382
00:36:08,560 --> 00:36:10,800
What kind of compliment
is "easy on the eyes"?

383
00:36:11,560 --> 00:36:14,000
It means she's pleasant to look at.

384
00:36:16,200 --> 00:36:18,280
Someone steady with a regular job is good.

385
00:36:19,040 --> 00:36:20,800
Don't date someone too domineering.

386
00:36:21,600 --> 00:36:22,680
We don't need that in this family.

387
00:36:24,400 --> 00:36:27,600
I'm choosing a girlfriend,
not a daughter-in-law for you.

388
00:36:28,200 --> 00:36:29,360
With your temper,

389
00:36:30,560 --> 00:36:31,520
you'll break up anyway.

390
00:36:32,600 --> 00:36:35,200
With your temper,
Mom still hasn't left you.

391
00:36:38,600 --> 00:36:40,040
All right, enough.

392
00:36:40,120 --> 00:36:41,320
This is good.

393
00:36:41,400 --> 00:36:44,240
I thought you'd be alone forever.

394
00:36:46,080 --> 00:36:48,280
A good personality matters.

395
00:36:48,920 --> 00:36:52,080
A girl may date you at first
because of your looks,

396
00:36:52,160 --> 00:36:56,320
but sooner or later,
she might not be able to stand you.

397
00:37:00,040 --> 00:37:03,120
By the way, Song Qiuhan's father told me

398
00:37:03,640 --> 00:37:05,960
your company was trying
to land Xingchi Auto as a client.

399
00:37:07,480 --> 00:37:08,560
We're working on it.

400
00:37:08,640 --> 00:37:10,080
How far along are you?

401
00:37:10,160 --> 00:37:14,040
In a deal of this size,
a proposal can only take you so far.

402
00:37:14,560 --> 00:37:15,560
People are what make deals happen.

403
00:37:16,840 --> 00:37:18,400
I know how to manage client relationships.

404
00:37:18,480 --> 00:37:20,160
Don't trouble yourself with it, Mr. Luan.

405
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:24,800
Don't let your talent make you arrogant.

406
00:37:25,480 --> 00:37:28,160
Creative ideas
aren't as valuable as you think.

407
00:37:28,240 --> 00:37:31,120
You need to spend more time
and put in more effort

408
00:37:31,200 --> 00:37:34,320
to understand what the client truly wants.

409
00:37:35,000 --> 00:37:35,880
Only then can you be sure of success.

410
00:37:35,960 --> 00:37:38,760
Why haven't you put this much effort
into Mom and me?

411
00:37:38,840 --> 00:37:40,680
Your own family
has never enjoyed that privilege.

412
00:37:41,280 --> 00:37:42,560
What nonsense are you talking about?

413
00:37:43,160 --> 00:37:44,720
I'm teaching you how to deal with people.

414
00:37:45,880 --> 00:37:48,400
If I hadn't been so strict
with you growing up

415
00:37:48,920 --> 00:37:50,120
and pushed you to become capable,

416
00:37:50,200 --> 00:37:51,800
would you be where you are today?

417
00:37:53,240 --> 00:37:54,920
Cacti can grow in the desert,

418
00:37:55,000 --> 00:37:57,800
but that doesn't mean
the desert is good for plants.

419
00:37:57,880 --> 00:37:59,800
- Hey you…
- All right, enough.

420
00:37:59,880 --> 00:38:00,720
Enough.

421
00:38:00,800 --> 00:38:02,920
It's Chinese New Year.
Why bring that up now?

422
00:38:03,000 --> 00:38:04,560
Our son is already doing very well.

423
00:38:04,640 --> 00:38:06,080
He doesn't need your guidance.

424
00:38:08,920 --> 00:38:09,960
Ignore him.

425
00:38:11,000 --> 00:38:12,560
Where are you going?

426
00:38:12,640 --> 00:38:14,680
Send me a photo of the girl.

427
00:38:14,760 --> 00:38:15,880
OK, I'll send you one.

428
00:38:15,960 --> 00:38:16,800
Hurry.

429
00:38:22,320 --> 00:38:23,320
Here it is.

430
00:38:26,840 --> 00:38:28,720
Look at what he sent me.

431
00:38:28,800 --> 00:38:30,240
Isn't that you?

432
00:38:30,320 --> 00:38:31,640
If he'd really wanted you to know,

433
00:38:32,320 --> 00:38:34,120
he would've sent you her photo long ago.

434
00:38:34,760 --> 00:38:37,000
You're always sticking
your nose into things.

435
00:38:37,080 --> 00:38:38,280
Can't I ask about my own son's

436
00:38:38,360 --> 00:38:39,800
- love life?
- What good does that do?

437
00:38:41,440 --> 00:38:43,280
He keeps brushing us off.

438
00:38:44,440 --> 00:38:47,600
You know perfectly well
he hates being interfered with

439
00:38:47,680 --> 00:38:49,760
and tied down, yet you still lecture him.

440
00:38:49,840 --> 00:38:51,800
Why can't I lecture him?

441
00:38:53,000 --> 00:38:56,240
He's been giving people
the silent treatment since childhood.

442
00:38:57,040 --> 00:38:58,080
What does he know about love?

443
00:38:58,160 --> 00:38:59,760
He knows nothing about it.

444
00:39:01,400 --> 00:39:05,800
I've also heard
he can be arrogant with clients

445
00:39:05,880 --> 00:39:06,720
and incredibly difficult to deal with.

446
00:39:07,320 --> 00:39:08,480
Who would like someone like that?

447
00:39:09,080 --> 00:39:11,200
People don't like him,
and he doesn't like people.

448
00:39:11,280 --> 00:39:12,360
Isn't that just perfect?

449
00:39:12,440 --> 00:39:13,560
Perfect?

450
00:39:15,320 --> 00:39:16,160
You've spoiled him.

451
00:39:16,240 --> 00:39:18,080
Why are you so annoying?

452
00:39:18,160 --> 00:39:19,920
Our son is right.

453
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:22,320
You should date someone
you enjoy looking at.

454
00:39:52,720 --> 00:39:54,480
<i>Go easier on my neck next time.</i>

455
00:39:58,120 --> 00:39:59,920
LUAN NIAN

456
00:40:07,200 --> 00:40:09,080
Why is it so quiet over there?

457
00:40:09,720 --> 00:40:12,240
<i>The firecrackers have</i>
<i>already started here.</i>

458
00:40:12,840 --> 00:40:14,320
My place is well soundproofed.

459
00:40:15,920 --> 00:40:17,120
What did you say?

460
00:40:17,840 --> 00:40:19,040
- <i>Hello?</i>
- Hello?

461
00:40:19,120 --> 00:40:21,440
- <i>Sweetheart, come set off fireworks!</i>
- <i>Coming!</i>

462
00:40:21,520 --> 00:40:24,320
I have to go. Bye.

463
00:40:34,440 --> 00:40:35,880
Happy Chinese New Year!

464
00:40:36,680 --> 00:40:39,160
Happy Chinese New Year!

465
00:40:39,240 --> 00:40:40,760
Happy Chinese New Year!

466
00:40:44,760 --> 00:40:46,200
They're beautiful.

467
00:40:48,200 --> 00:40:49,680
So beautiful!

468
00:40:52,080 --> 00:40:53,560
Happy Chinese New Year!

469
00:40:54,160 --> 00:40:55,000
Your red envelope.

470
00:40:57,120 --> 00:40:59,280
Come on. Family photo.

471
00:41:15,240 --> 00:41:16,440
<i>Come back to Beijing soon.</i>

472
00:41:58,440 --> 00:41:59,880
BOARDING GATES

473
00:42:04,160 --> 00:42:05,520
You've got to hand it to Luke.

474
00:42:05,600 --> 00:42:07,440
He picked Phuket for the company retreat.

475
00:42:07,520 --> 00:42:08,520
Yeah.

476
00:42:11,280 --> 00:42:12,240
Lumi.

477
00:42:13,600 --> 00:42:15,560
Why aren't you wearing
the dress I bought you?

478
00:42:15,640 --> 00:42:16,960
You're not wearing yours either.

479
00:42:17,040 --> 00:42:18,080
Mine's in my suitcase.

480
00:42:18,160 --> 00:42:19,040
So is mine.

481
00:42:19,120 --> 00:42:19,960
Alright.

482
00:42:20,040 --> 00:42:21,400
Then we'll change when we get there.

483
00:42:21,480 --> 00:42:22,320
Sit here.

484
00:42:23,040 --> 00:42:24,120
Where's your seat?

485
00:42:24,200 --> 00:42:25,400
- My seat…
- Look.

486
00:42:26,640 --> 00:42:27,680
Isn't that Luke?

487
00:42:29,360 --> 00:42:31,840
He's not joining us
on this southern tour, is he?

488
00:42:31,920 --> 00:42:34,080
Wouldn't that mean overtime in Phuket?

489
00:42:34,160 --> 00:42:35,320
No way.

490
00:42:35,400 --> 00:42:37,800
Why would he come on our company retreat?

491
00:42:37,880 --> 00:42:41,040
Probably because I'm the boss,
and I can go wherever I want.

492
00:42:44,440 --> 00:42:45,720
Where are you going?

493
00:42:46,920 --> 00:42:48,120
On the company retreat.

494
00:42:49,000 --> 00:42:50,080
You're coming with us?

495
00:42:50,160 --> 00:42:51,600
Is there a problem?

496
00:42:56,720 --> 00:42:57,760
Then…

497
00:42:58,320 --> 00:42:59,840
why aren't you in the first-class lounge?

498
00:42:59,920 --> 00:43:02,800
Since this is a company retreat,
there'll be no special treatment.

499
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:06,840
Can I sit here?

500
00:43:08,160 --> 00:43:09,360
Let's move it.

501
00:43:10,680 --> 00:43:11,520
Go ahead.

502
00:43:18,240 --> 00:43:20,520
Could you be any more inconsiderate?

503
00:43:21,240 --> 00:43:23,480
How are we supposed
to have fun with you there?

504
00:43:24,760 --> 00:43:26,240
Then don't go.

505
00:43:37,960 --> 00:43:39,080
Why do you keep looking at me?

506
00:43:40,080 --> 00:43:42,040
It's not like I refused to get you
a business-class seat.

507
00:43:45,440 --> 00:43:47,160
I'll upgrade you now.

508
00:43:49,360 --> 00:43:51,560
Come on. Help me see
if we can upgrade his seat.

509
00:43:55,560 --> 00:43:57,960
<i>Passengers traveling to Phuket,</i>

510
00:43:58,040 --> 00:44:01,360
<i>please gather your belongings</i>
<i>and prepare to board.</i>

511
00:44:27,400 --> 00:44:28,240
You're awake?

512
00:44:30,680 --> 00:44:32,960
Here. Have some water.

513
00:44:49,360 --> 00:44:50,200
Your fever's gone down.

514
00:44:50,720 --> 00:44:52,680
If it comes back tomorrow,

515
00:44:53,200 --> 00:44:54,080
you'll still need a shot
to bring the fever down.

516
00:44:56,560 --> 00:44:58,240
Ask Alex for leave.

517
00:44:58,880 --> 00:45:00,240
Take five full days off.

518
00:45:02,560 --> 00:45:03,840
I don't need that many days.

519
00:45:06,560 --> 00:45:07,600
I still have work to do.

520
00:45:07,680 --> 00:45:10,600
Once the fever fries your brain,
you won't have to work at all.

521
00:45:14,560 --> 00:45:15,880
I'll rest at home.

522
00:45:32,040 --> 00:45:33,440
I know you have something to say.

523
00:45:34,640 --> 00:45:35,480
I'm going out for a while.

524
00:45:35,560 --> 00:45:38,560
Think about how you want to say it
before I get back.
